    "multi_column_bVGh8q": {
      "type": "multi-column",
      "blocks": {
        "item_MCzkPF": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "column_size": "3",
            "title": "1. Wooden Box Fermentation",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<p>Fresh beans are transported to the Los Arroyos fermentorium. Here, natural microbial activity in wooden boxes breaks down sugars, unlocking the raw seeds' complex flavor precursors.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_fDALTw": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "column_size": "3",
            "title": "2. Controlled Drying",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<p>The fermented beans undergo a meticulous drying process, bringing moisture levels down <strong>from 50% to an optimal 7%</strong>. This crucial step refines the flavor profile and eliminates harsh bitterness.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_Tp3hLN": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "column_size": "3",
            "title": "3. Varietal Selection",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "content": "<p>Featuring restored groves dominated by Amelonado ancestry, the cacao is carefully sorted to ensure only the highest quality beans make it to production, guaranteeing a rich, balanced base.</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        }
      },
